-- Headings that are more than one plain word (overnight card O6, 2026-10-11).
-- `Part 1. Fees` holds a space and a dot, so `presumed` names its rule the way
-- L4 spells a qualified name in an ambiguity error, with backticks round the
-- parts that need them, and a reader can still tell the heading from the rule.

@export default Combine
GIVEN useAlpha IS A BOOLEAN
      useBeta  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS
  (IF useAlpha THEN `Part 1. Fees`.scaled WITH base IS 10 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF useBeta THEN `Part 2`.scaled WITH base IS 10 ELSE 0)

§ `Part 1. Fees`

DECLARE Config
  HAS timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
      retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

§ `Part 2`

DECLARE Config
  HAS timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 60
      retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base
